[1K Recorded incremental demo. Start from identified plain llama.cpp cf34d3113 (owned checkout,[3;101H[1K branch `demo-incremental`) and the frozen fast contract qwen36-quick-v1. Use[4;101H[1K engine.expert_streaming as your engineering method: read its guide and the current evidence, then[5;101H[1K make one meaningful behavioural change at a time. For every decision write the mechanism[6;101H[1K hypothesis and why the chosen component fits it in `hypothesis`, and in `uncertainty` name what[7;101H[1K is still unknown plus one alternative you are deferring and why. Candidates, not predetermined[8;101H[1K winners: demand fill first (expert_fill, with its source prerequisites installed but their[9;101H[1K switches off), then predictive reads (expert_pregate) only if the fill evidence supports[10;101H[1K continuing. For each intervention: integrate, build once through the builder (never rebuild[11;101H[1K unchanged source), run one cheap screen (a single lab run: output identity and engagement; its[12;101H[1K timing is preliminary), then if the screen passes run one 1-round ABBA against the current best[13;101H[1K under the same contract and keep or revert by the component's acceptance rule. Do not group[14;101H[1K unrelated active optimizations and do not tune parameters. After the last keep, run one 1-round[15;101H[1K ABBA of the plain baseline image versus the final image as the headline comparison, then finish[16;101H[1K with accept, reject or report_inconclusive and a short report of ms/token per arm, output[17;101H[1K identity and engagement.[18;101H[1K
